WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.167
Logistic regression.

2
00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.512
Despite the name, it classifies.

3
00:00:04.512 --> 00:00:07.900
And its real gift is a probability, not just a label.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.367
Here is the pipeline.

5
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.600
Start with the features of a planet.

6
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.433
A linear model turns them into one raw score.

7
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:19.333
The sigmoid squashes that score into the range zero to one.

8
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:21.300
And out comes a probability.

9
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.067
This is the sigmoid curve.

10
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:29.857
Very negative scores flatten toward zero, very positive scores flatten toward one.

11
00:00:29.857 --> 00:00:32.067
Any score lands strictly between.

12
00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.921
A score of zero gives exactly one half.

13
00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:39.900
Above the threshold, which defaults to zero point five, we predict positive.

14
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.867
Here it is as an equation.

15
00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:44.600
Compute the raw linear score.

16
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.367
Push it through the sigmoid.

17
00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:50.000
And the result is the probability of the positive class.

18
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.500
In scikit-learn, we train it and ask for probabilities.

19
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.267
Fit on the training data.

20
00:00:56.567 --> 00:01:00.033
Predict proba returns the chance each planet is a candidate.

21
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:03.600
Plain predict applies the zero point five threshold.

22
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.000
And the coefficients show which features push toward the class.

23
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.600
Now the real scenario.

24
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.780
Telescope time is limited.

25
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:18.000
A zero point five one and a zero point nine seven candidate are both labeled positive.

26
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:24.928
But if you sort by probability instead, the near certain candidates get observed first and the coin flips wait.

27
00:01:24.928 --> 00:01:26.600
That ranking comes for free.

28
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:28.504
Let's recap.

29
00:01:28.504 --> 00:01:30.733
A linear score goes through a sigmoid.

30
00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.833
The output is a probability.

31
00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.000
A threshold turns it into a label.

32
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.500
And you should rank by probability, not by label.

33
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.067
Next up: decision trees.
